that God believes <em>T </em>infallibly, but that God believed
<em>T</em> <em>yesterday</em>. This solution probably originated with
the 6<sup>th</sup> century philosopher Boethius, who maintained that
God is not in time and has no temporal properties, so God does not
have beliefs at a time. It is therefore a mistake to say God had
beliefs yesterday, or has beliefs today, or will have beliefs
tomorrow. It is also a mistake to say God had a belief on a certain
date, such as June 1, 2004. The way Boethius describes Godâ€™s
