<p>
Since the nature of the timeless realm is elusive, the intuition of
the necessity of the timeless realm is probably weaker than the
intuition of the necessity of the past, so the availability of a
timeless version of the argument for theological fatalism isnâ€™t
necessarily fatal to the Boethian solution. The necessity of the past
