<h3 id="MoliSolu">2.5 The dependence solution</h3>

<p>
One of the best-known Ockhamist proposals after Adams was made by
Alvin Plantinga (1986), who defined the accidentally necessary in
terms of lack of counterfactual power. For someone, Jones, to have
counterfactual power over Godâ€™s past beliefs, the following must
be true:</p>

<dl class="sentag tag3em">
<dt>(CPP)</dt>
<dd>It was within Jonesâ€™ power at <em>t</em><sub>2</sub> to do
something such that if he did it, God would not have held the belief
