certain belief at <em>t</em><sub>1</sub>, and then Jones does
something to make a different past. That requires two pasts prior to
<em>t</em><sub>2</sub>, and that presumably makes no sense. What (CPP)
affirms instead is that there is only one actual past, but there would
have been a different past if Jones acted differently at
<em>t</em><sub>2</sub>. (CPP) also does not require the assumption
